# ============================================================================
# NekoGo publish rules (Nov 2026)
#
# Every rule above this line came from the Qt NekoBox tree, where nothing
# named *.json was ever source. NekoGo is Go + Vue, and the blanket *.json
# silently hollowed out the repo: gui/frontend/package.json,
# package-lock.json, tsconfig.json and gui/wails.json were never committed,
# so a fresh clone cannot npm install - and therefore cannot produce
# gui/frontend/dist, which main.go embeds at compile time - nor run
# wails3 generate bindings. The blanket *.dll hid runtime/WinDivert.dll for
# the same reason: build.bat copies it with `if exist`, so a clone without it
# prints BUILD OK and ships an install whose SNI-spoofing engine cannot load
# its driver. Last rule wins, so this block re-includes what the build needs
# and ignores the reference and scratch trees that a git add -A would sweep
# in (PattN, the source* exports, backups and the upload output are
# hundreds of megabytes of other people's trees and old copies).
# ============================================================================

# Build inputs the extension rules above were hiding. node_modules, target
# and dist are excluded as directories further down, and git cannot
# re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so these negations
# reach the real source trees only.
!**/package.json
!**/package-lock.json
!**/tsconfig*.json
!**/wails.json
!runtime/WinDivert.dll

# The Psiphon server list gui/psiphon_servers.go embeds. Without it the
# build cannot compile, and the "bundled server list" option has nothing
# to hand the core.
!gui/psiphon_servers.dat

# Generated, and recreated by the build: npm run build, cargo build,
# go generate (rsrc.syso) and build.bat itself
node_modules/
target/
dist/
gui/build/
gui/dist/
gui/frontend/dist/
*.syso

# Licensed data fetched by build.bat, never source
*.mmdb

# Not this project's source: a vendored clone (build.bat fetches Xray-core
# when missing) and the reference trees read-only by policy
/xray/
/PattN/
/Throne/
/aether-reference/bin/

# Local output and old copies of this tree, all regenerable
/source*/
/NekoGo-upload/
/nekogo-backup/
/dist/

# Never publish: the user's own subscription data (spoof_config.txt is a dump
# of live links with real passwords, and it sat inside the exported tree until
# Nov 2026) and the machine-local upload settings, which carry a repo path and
# a proxy endpoint.
spoof_config.txt
.uploadrc.json

# Internal development log, not documentation for users
AGENT_LOG.md
